  "details": "Why:\n\nPreviously, \"Photos are sorted into folders by year and month\" was displayed, for now, the path of the VRChat photo storage folder is displayed.\n\nI think it has two problems:\n\n- Some people might be doxxed their real name via screenshots or screen recording\n\n- Even if you're in streamer mode, it will keep displaying\n\nThe first, the photos taken with VRChat are saved in \"Pictures\\VRChat\", but mostly saved through Windows user folders (C:\\Users\\<UserName>\\Pictures\\VRChat). so here's the problem. many people set their real name as the user folder name. I'm afraid some people might be doxxed their real name via screenshots or something.\n\nBtw, modern Windows uses the last five digits of the Microsoft account email address for the user folder name when you log in to your Microsoft account during setup.\n\nThe second has a similar reason to the first too, but if VRChat Dev decides that this change isn't reverted, at the least, it shouldn't be displayed in streamer mode.\n\nI don't think it should continue like this. so, I want to ask for change.\n\nThere are two solutions:\n\n- Revert this change\n\n- change the visibility to off by default then force visibility off in streamer mode",
